pve-storage-drs (0.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * `collect-testdata`'s diagnostic bundle no longer leaks a live cluster's
    unconfigured Prometheus/Telegraf labels (a real guest hostname, seen via
    a `host` tag) into `findings.json`'s free-text "sample series labels"
    finding -- found by hand-reading a fresh corpus submission before
    treating it as clean. The message is now rebuilt from the same
    vmid/device/node-only view already used for the structured field next
    to it, instead of trying to redact an open-ended raw label dict as free
    text.
  * `verify-metrics`/`show-load`/`plan` no longer silently read zero
    coverage and zero load against a gigapipe deployment whose
    `/api/v1/query_range` (and the PromQL subquery form) returns no series
    at all whenever a query's own step is `>=` the range-vector duration of
    the `rate()`-family function inside it -- confirmed live on two
    independent gigapipe deployments, and exactly the boundary this
    project's own default config (`metrics.step` == `metrics.rate_window`)
    sits on. A new workaround (`metrics.safe_range_step_seconds()`/
    `decimate_to_configured_step()`) requests a smaller, whole-second step
    when needed and decimates the denser response back down, with no
    effect on an unaffected backend and no effect on replaying a bundle
    captured before this fix existed.

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bzed@debian.org>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:11:16 +0200

pve-storage-drs (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * REVIEW.md sixteenth-pass fixes (findings Y-01..Y-07), verifying the
    fifteenth pass's own X-01..X-10 fixes: a diagnostic bundle's
    `manifest.json` no longer risks a mangled PVE/Prometheus version string
    (the vmid-redaction pass could rewrite a digit run inside it, e.g.
    `pve-manager/8.2.11` with vmid 11 registered); the corpus scrub audit's
    own backstop for an unredacted transport-failure hostname no longer
    flags the collector's *correctly* redacted `host='<redacted>'`
    sentinel, which would otherwise have failed the corpus gate on the
    first real bundle to hit a connection blip; and the corpus's narrow
    sweep now reports a skipped solver backend as "not swept without
    --full-matrix" unconditionally, rather than a label that depended on
    whether the CI/build environment happened to have that solver
    installed. Three documentation corrections: the collect-testdata
    worked example's sample-points figure, IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md section
    16.6's regression-file field list, and its estimate-printing claim, all
    brought in line with as-built behaviour.
  * README.md gains an AI-disclaimer section, naming the models used for
    planning, implementation and automated review.

