pve-storage-drs (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Disk-size resolution (topology.py) fixed against three live-cluster
    incidents: a content-listing entry present but missing its own `size`
    no longer crashes (falls back to the VM config's size=, warning
    named); a size-less entry's approximate-size (PVE 9.2+, qcow2 on
    shared LVM) is now preferred over that fallback; and a managed disk's
    exact size is now queried from its own VM's node rather than an
    arbitrary node reporting the storage active, since only the node with
    the volume's LV active can report it.
  * REVIEW.md fourteenth-pass fixes (findings W-01..W-09), and the
    operator correction that followed: a cluster-naming-label query-scoping
    tier was added on this pass's own mistaken assumption that such a label
    is a fixed deployment convention -- it was not, and has been removed
    again in full (metrics.labels.cluster, its discovery scan, and the
    degrade-on-denied-Sys.Audit handling are all gone; querying stays
    scoped by node list, or by metrics.extra_selector when set). What
    survives from W-07: show-load/gates.py still name a query filter that
    matched no series at all explicitly, instead of reporting the group
    idle. Plus five documentation-residue fixes that still apply: the
    operator manual's stale "`auto` not yet" status-page parenthetical,
    changelog phase mislabelling, a stale topology stage count and dead
    function name, the operator manual's warnings paragraph (now covers
    all four size-resolution warnings), and the read-path call-count
    formula (W-01..W-05).
  * New: `collect-testdata` captures an anonymized diagnostic bundle from a
    real cluster (PVE inventory plus a Prometheus superset, salted
    HMAC pseudonyms for every vmid/node/storage/tag, timestamps rebased off
    the real date) for the author to debug against; `--replay <bundle>`
    reruns any read-only subcommand against a captured bundle with no
    network access at all (apply and escalated --mode are refused). Four
    new `support.*` config knobs govern it. See
    docs/manual/26-collect-testdata-and-replay.md and
    IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md section 16.
  * New: tests/corpus/, a suite of real (anonymized) cluster bundles
    exercised by `make check` (scrub audit, safety invariants,
    MILP-vs-heuristic comparison, plan regression) and by `make corpus`
    (the full solver/forecast/backend matrix) -- the largest-scale
    correctness check this project has, run against real cluster shapes
    instead of only tests/fixtures/*.yaml's synthetic ones.
  * Logging policy re-plan and implementation (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
    section 2.3): a clean run is silent by default; apply --mode
    confirm|auto always emits its unattended audit trail regardless of
    verbosity (only --quiet suppresses it); -v/-vv name third-party
    library noise without promoting it past WARNING; --json keeps the
    report on stdout and every log record on stderr; --log-format/
    --log-level are new global options.
  * json_safe(): --json output and every log record now reject
    Infinity/NaN (RFC 8259) instead of emitting them -- fixes a real
    +inf payback ratio on every no-move ACT run.
  * verify-metrics gains a cross-metric consistency check: Telegraf's
    Prometheus-compatible output silently drops a field the moment it
    observes one non-numeric value for it, which can hit exactly one of
    the six configured metrics for one disk while the coverage check's own
    read_ops-only probe stays clean -- found on a second production
    cluster's metrics pipeline switch, fixed the same day (REVIEW.md
    section 28).
  * explain gains a closest-rejected-move section: when a group's
    objective is lowest doing nothing, explain now also reports the best
    single-disk move that was considered and rejected, and by how much it
    would have made things worse.
  * New docs: a real quickstart (docs/manual/00-installation.md) and
    docs/manual/05-metrics-pipeline.md, documenting the
    InfluxDB-line-protocol-to-Prometheus type trap and naming the tested
    metrics-transport backend; the Markdown sources of all three documents
    now ship alongside their PDFs.

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bzed@debian.org>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 10:41:49 +0200

pve-storage-drs (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First functional implementation: all nine IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md phases
    are now built and wired into the CLI, closing out the "not yet
    buildable" state of 0.0.1.
    - config.py, units.py, forecast.py, logging_setup.py (phase 1): config
      loading/validation, duration/size parsing, and quantile/
      seasonal_naive/holt_winters forecasting.
    - metrics.py (phase 1) and pve.py (phase 2): the Prometheus client and
      PromQL, and the Proxmox VE API client (proxmoxer-based).
    - topology.py (phase 2): the disk/storage/group join driving
      show-load and verify-storages.
    - gates.py (phase 3): the act/no-act decision (reserve override,
      drift, imbalance).
    - heuristic.py (phase 4, dependency-free) and optimize.py (phase 6,
      CP-SAT/CBC MILP backends): two interchangeable solvers behind
      solver.backend: auto/heuristic/cpsat/cbc.
    - schedule.py and payback.py (phase 5): move ordering/pacing and the
      benefit-vs-cost gate a plan must clear before it is offered.
    - execute.py (phase 7, section 11.2 state.json): dry-run/confirm/auto
      execution, drift history and gates.cooldown_per_disk/
      cooldown_per_storage tracking, and crash-recovery from an in-flight
      move.
    - auto mode and execution.time_windows (phase 8): unattended
      operation, the migration cap and the re-plan loop.
    - forecast.py's seasonal-naive model, validated by backtest beyond
      quantile/p95 (phase 9).
  * explain: the diagnostic subcommand -- measured load, pinned disks with
    per-pin action hints, fragmentation, the objective's five terms, and
    the pinned-load-fraction warning.
  * All six subcommands (show-load, verify-metrics, verify-storages, plan,
    apply, explain) are implemented and documented; none report "not
    implemented yet" any longer.
  * Full documentation set: docs/manual (operator reference) and
    docs/internals (implementation reference) now cover every module and
    CLI subcommand, alongside IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md itself; all three are
    built to PDF and committed with sha256 freshness stamps.
  * Hardened through REVIEW.md passes 1-13 (findings F-01 through V-05):
    config edge cases, PromQL correctness, PVE API privilege requirements,
    disk-bus/snapshot/lock handling, payback and scheduling fixes, cooldown
    and state-tracking corrections, and plain-language runtime messages.
  * Packaging: debian/control, debian/rules, debian/tests and the
    autopkgtest (installed-package smoke test) now match a real,
    importable package; both GitHub Actions and the GitLab/Salsa pipeline
    (sbuild, lintian, piuparts, reprotest, autopkgtest) exercise it.
  * python3-pulp and coinor-cbc moved from Recommends to Depends: a real
    MILP solver (CBC) is now installed by default, rather than left to the
    operator to add. The dependency-free heuristic (IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
    section 5.5) remains a genuine fallback for a non-Debian install with
    no solver, or when a solve fails or times out; CP-SAT (ortools) stays
    an optional pip-only extra, unpackaged for Debian.
  * Dogfooded against a real Proxmox VE 9.2 cluster and Prometheus
    instance; no known outstanding correctness findings.

